// ============================================================================
//  GAMETYPE DEFINITION RAWFILES
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  🛑 CORRECTS THE DELIVERY METHOD USED IN v1.6.1.
//
//  v1.6.1 put these .txt files in mod.iwd. That does not work: verified after
//  deploying, the files were confirmed present inside mod.iwd and the engine
//  STILL logged, on every map load,
//
//      Could not load rawfile "maps/mp/gametypes_zm/zmeat.txt"
//      Could not load rawfile "maps/mp/gametypes_zm/zrace.txt"
//      Could not load rawfile "maps/mp/gametypes_zm/zturned.txt"
//
//  So mod.iwd serves SCRIPTS (Plutonium's Mods loader reads raw .gsc from it -
//  that is how ridgelandproject.gsc works) but NOT rawfile assets. Rawfiles have
//  to come out of mod.ff, exactly like animtrees/zm_buried_ghost.atr above.
//  The mode .gsc scripts stay in mod.iwd, where scripts do load from.
//
//  _gametypes.txt is the master list the engine walks. Declaring ours overrides
//  the stock one, which matters for more than tidiness: the stock list names the
//  containment mode "zcontainment" (hence the log asking for zcontainment.txt)
//  while Reimagined's file - and its gametypestable - call it "zcontain". With
//  our list in force the engine asks for the names we actually ship.
//
//  Sourced from zone_assets\maps\mp\gametypes_zm\.
//
//  NOTE: this makes the gametypes LOADABLE. It does NOT put them in the menu -
//  that still needs zm\gametypestable.csv as a stringtable, the localized
//  strings, and the LUI gameTypes arrays. See checkpoint 10 section 8.
// ============================================================================
rawfile,maps/mp/gametypes_zm/_gametypes.txt
rawfile,maps/mp/gametypes_zm/zmeat.txt
rawfile,maps/mp/gametypes_zm/zrace.txt
rawfile,maps/mp/gametypes_zm/zturned.txt
rawfile,maps/mp/gametypes_zm/zcontain.txt
rawfile,maps/mp/gametypes_zm/zsr.txt

// ============================================================================
//  BURIED ZOMBIE XMODELS  -  fixes the Borough crash
//        AimTarget_GetTagPos: Cannot find tag [j_helmet] on entity of type [16]
//        COM_ERROR (1) / SV_Shutdown, a minute or two into the round.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  v1.13.0 got the nine aitypes loading (the log confirms all nine as "(mod)")
//  and the spawner entities into the base mapents, so zombies finally spawn on
//  Borough. They spawn with NO USABLE MODEL, though, and that is what crashes.
//
//  Declaring aitype/character/xmodelalias SCRIPTS was only half the job. Those
//  scripts setmodel() actual xmodel assets, and per the Unlinker every single one
//  of them lives ONLY in so_zclassic_zm_buried.ff:
//
//        xmodel c_zom_zombie_buried_*   in zm_buried.ff (base)  ->   0
//        xmodel c_zom_zombie_buried_*   in so_zclassic_zm_buried.ff -> 118
//
//  A zstandard game loads the base map but not the zclassic addon, so the model
//  never resolves, the actor has no skeleton, and the first time aim assist tries
//  to read the j_helmet tag off one the game hard-errors. It is the exact same
//  gap as the ghost animtree and the player characters above - just caught one
//  layer later, because a script that is present but points at an absent xmodel
//  fails silently until something touches the model.
//
//  All 118 are declared, not just the bodies: the set includes heads, hair, hats
//  and the g_* gib models, and a missing gib model would fault the same way the
//  moment a limb comes off.
//
//  🛑 NOT verified in game yet.
// ============================================================================
xmodel,c_zom_zombie_buried_civilian_body1
xmodel,c_zom_zombie_buried_civilian_body2
xmodel,c_zom_zombie_buried_civilian_body2_nohat
xmodel,c_zom_zombie_buried_civilian_body3
xmodel,c_zom_zombie_buried_civilian_body3_nohat
